I've started eight research agents in parallel, one per vendor: Linear, Notion, Figma, Vercel, Intercom, Retool, Airtable and Loom. Loom's list may now be on atlassian.com since Atlassian acquired it. Each agent is looking for the vendor's own subprocessor page and pulling:
- the exact page URL;
- the full list and an exact count, broken down by table where a page has more than one;
- every subprocessor located outside the US/EU, with the UK, Switzerland and the rest of the EEA marked separately because they're borderline;
- the "last updated" date, quoted word for word, or a clear statement that the page doesn't show one.

When they've all reported back, I'll put the results into one table with a source URL for every fact.

